From: ProjectM TV contributors
Subject: [PROPOSAL] Retain instance thick flags and safely group disconnected Native outlines

Capture evaluated int-nonzero thick once per instance. Preserve existing
I23 widths/offsets/pass order, floating RGBA, positive-only file booleans,
fill calls, bounded batches and prepared replay. Group only contiguous
thick/untextured/zero-fill/finite instances with pairwise disjoint expanded
raster bounds, same blend destination, maximum16 per group. Do not group
overlap, opaque/textured fills, missing borders or different styles.

Pack explicit four-point segment neighbours in a suffix of the existing
line VBO, preserving disconnection and per-instance float colours. No new
shader or GPU buffer. No-group uploads keep their original fast path.
City-lights' four separated transparent thick outlines then use four
Native calls total rather than16, while authored still needs16 loops.
Packing, bounded overlap tests, extra upload calls and scratch memory are
new work: Native/cost acceptance remains open.

Original: milkdropfs.cpp:2454/2510; geometric/source policy, not D3D pixels.

